---
description: Deploy via deploy.bat after app-affecting edits unless the user opts out for that turn.
alwaysApply: true
---

When a turn changes **app-affecting** files, end the turn by running **only** `deploy.bat` from the repo root (do not run separate `dotnet clean` / `dotnet build` / `dotnet publish` steps).

**Deploy when you change any of:**
- `src/Eve-F-Preview/**` (C#, designer, resx, icons, csproj, manifest, etc.)
- `src/EVE-F-Preview.sln` or other files that affect the built executable
- `deploy.bat` itself (only if you need to verify the deploy script)

**Do not deploy for:**
- Docs (`README.md`, `TESTING-*.md`, `LICENSE`, etc.)
- Scripts used for release/ops only (`create-release.ps1`, tools scripts)
- Config samples / JSON next to the repo that are not compiled in
- Cursor rules (`.cursor/**`), git metadata, assets not embedded in the app
- Turns that only answer questions and touch no app files

**Exception:** Skip deploy if the user explicitly says not to deploy in that turn (e.g. “don’t deploy”, “skip deploy”, “no deploy”).

```
deploy.bat
```

Or from PowerShell:

```powershell
cd "C:\Users\cmatt\Documents\Code\farfnarkle\eve-f-preview"
.\deploy.bat
```

`deploy.bat` builds Release, publishes the single-file exe, stops any running `EVE-F-Preview.exe` gracefully (so settings can save), copies **only** the exe to `C:\Eve\EVE-F-Preview.exe`, and starts it. It must never overwrite `C:\Eve\EVE-F-Preview.json`.

Report success or errors. On success, mention:

- Published: `C:\Users\cmatt\Documents\Code\farfnarkle\eve-f-preview\bin\net8.0-windows8.0\win-x64\publish\EVE-F-Preview.exe`
- Deployed: `C:\Eve\EVE-F-Preview.exe`
